CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Giving the examples of Raymond Branch and Dora Lopez as support
 \, Brandt argues that race and class impact how much access people have to
  literacy sponsorship. Summarize the kinds of access Branch and Lopez had-
 -for example\, in their early education\, access to books and computers\, 
 and parental support--and decide whether or not you agree with Brandt's cl
 aim. Be sure to support your argument with clear\, specific examples.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Discussion Post due Sept. 8: Brandt\, "Sponsors of Literacy"--Part 
 I [ERH-101-22-FL26]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://vmi.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course_
 25748&month=09&year=2026#assignment_296519
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>Giving the examples of Raymond Branch and D
 ora Lopez as support\, Brandt argues that race and class impact how much a
 ccess people have to literacy sponsorship. Summarize the kinds of access B
 ranch and Lopez had--for example\, in their early education\, access to bo
 oks and computers\, and parental support--and decide whether or not you ag
 ree with Brandt's claim. Be sure to support your argument with clear\, spe
 cific examples.</p>
END:VEVENT
